      'Classes run nine to three on the class days: the year’s courses, each training one of those skills. Be there, in New Haven and awake, and your craft grows, more when you come rested. You began among the class’s strongest, not ahead of everyone: your fifteen classmates grow too, each at their own pace, and you’re cast beside and against them. Unwell or down with the flu, Call In Sick before the classes begin, at the latest when the clock stops at them at nine, and the day’s classes, labs and rehearsal calls are excused; a work-study shift isn’t. A day in hospital is excused of itself. Staying away when you’re well is an absence.',
